  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The central iodine atom undergoes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>&nbsp;hybridization and has&nbsp;3&nbsp;lone pairs of electrons and&nbsp;2&nbsp;bond pairs of electrons.</p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>&nbsp;has trigonal bipyramidal geometry and linear shape .</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0177_a20547d8ec2c.png\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 139px;\" /></p><p>Shape : Linear, I-I-I Bond angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"
